WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.188
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.188 --> 00:00:14.265
Today, resources: health, stamina, and anything else your characters can run out of.

5
00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:17.866
Open Mechanics, then Resources.

6
00:00:17.866 --> 00:00:20.846
These are the bars on a character's sheet.

7
00:00:20.846 --> 00:00:25.174
Voyage gives you health, and I've added stamina for our acts.

8
00:00:25.174 --> 00:00:26.522
Let's open stamina.

9
00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:33.242
The description is for players: they read it from the little info icon on their character sheet.

10
00:00:33.242 --> 00:00:35.988
The AI reads something else, further down.

11
00:00:36.433 --> 00:00:41.303
Recharge per turn is how much comes back on its own, and it has to be a whole number.

12
00:00:41.303 --> 00:00:44.626
Increase per level is added to the maximum every level up.

13
00:00:44.626 --> 00:00:48.694
And restored on rest is how much comes back on a rest: all of it, here.

14
00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:53.544
Starting value and maximum value are where a new character begins.

15
00:00:53.544 --> 00:00:59.357
The maximum isn't a hard ceiling: traits, attributes and levels all raise it from here.

16
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.348
Usage instructions are what the AI actually reads.

17
00:01:03.348 --> 00:01:06.896
Voyage's docs suggest three parts: what spends it,

18
00:01:06.896 --> 00:01:11.437
a list of costs from minor to extreme, and when not to take any.

19
00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:16.333
Skip that last list and the AI might drain stamina over a quiet chat.

20
00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:20.312
And is health marks the bar that combat damages.

21
00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:23.119
When it hits zero, the character dies.

22
00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:27.181
Set it on exactly one resource, and here that's health.

23
00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:30.591
Health grows on its own schedule.

24
00:01:30.591 --> 00:01:35.559
Start at the maximum, add the increase per level for every level after the first,

25
00:01:35.559 --> 00:01:38.565
and every fifth level throws in five more on top.

26
00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:41.999
That last bit is built into Voyage, you can't change it.

27
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.403
Two more tricks.

28
00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:50.169
A tracker, like luck or reputation, is a resource with no recharge and nothing back on rest,

29
00:01:50.169 --> 00:01:52.989
and the usage instructions say what moves it.

30
00:01:52.989 --> 00:01:56.625
And when you need an exact change, not the AI's judgement,

31
00:01:56.625 --> 00:01:59.445
that's a job for triggers, later this season.

32
00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:01.968
That's resources.

33
00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:04.972
Our stamina bar is linked in the description.

34
00:02:04.972 --> 00:02:08.577
Next time, traits: the pages of the character creator.

35
00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:12.981
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

